e of  Valhalla eight of those episodes are  already reserved for the first season  and it's unclear how many episodes  subsequent seasons will be either way  the sheer size of the order speaks  volumes about the company's belief in  the series which is a smart play  considering the original series had a  sixth season run that spanned 89  episodes if there's one thing that  Vikings has been great at doing is  killing off its main characters season 3  saw the deaths of Earl haroldson's Widow  rollo's girlfriend Siggy and the priest  Ragnar's BFF athelston Viking season 4  knocked off Ragnar's second wife ausleg  his friend and rival King Egbert and  most shockingly of all Ragnar himself  who up until that point had been the  series main protagonist in season 5 as  more characters were added the bodies  continued to pile up it has been  confirmed that the new series will take  place around 100 years after the current  show so even the youngest Vikings  characters will be dead and gone by then  naturally Vikings Valhalla will feature  all new characters based on even more  historical figures from Norse Legend  further Hollywood Reporter some of the  main characters of Vikings Valhalla will  be Leif Ericsson Freitas Eric's daughter  Harold sigurdson Emma of Normandy and  King knuts the great Leif Erikson is  arguably the most famous of the larts he  has a pretty big claim to fame as he's  believed to be the first European to  discover North America rather than  Christopher Columbus not only that but  Leif Erikson is said to have done so a  whole half Millennium before Columbus  sailed the ocean blue setting foot in a  land he dubbed Finland back in the 11th  century then there's greatest life's  sister who's also said to have taken  part in the Finland Voyage though her  historical record is spotty she's always  portrayed as a fierce Warrior Vikings  Valhalla will almost certainly include  the sibling's trip to the New World In  His plot next is Harold hardrada born  about 45 years after Leif Erikson he's  regarded as the last great Viking leader  having fought for control of Norway and  Denmark before meeting his end during an  invasion of England his successor in  some respects was his contemporary the  Norman King William the Conqueror who  wasn't a viking but claimed Viking  ancestry as a descendant of the one and  only Rollo William conquered England  following Harold hardrada's defeat  becoming its king the pair's respective  battles were almost certainly factor  into the plot of Vikings Valhalla all  the same Netflix released the Show's  first trailer which is in a word  riveting naturally the trailer kicks off  with the Vikings at Sea during a rip  roaring storm and if the rest of the  footage is any indication there will be  a plethora of battle scenes which is  likely what fans of Vikings ordered up  in their dreams with Valhalla set to  premiere Friday February 25th on Netflix  audience members still have time to  watch the original series all the same  be prepared to travel the hair raising  seas and charge the bloody battlefields  with Viking Legends  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more Looper videos about  your favorite TV shows are coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the Bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

